{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1794539679, "title": "dev/cycling-prototype \u00b7 ambitious run 1", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "theme": {"fg": "#d8dee9", "bg": "#1e1f1c", "palette": "#272822:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f8f8f2:#75715e:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f9f8f5"}}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Build a clickable prototype of the app in plan.md that I can open as a single html file\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.948, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && ls -la && cat plan.md)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[94.144, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command, wrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/prototype.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[96.445, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 2 shell commands, wrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && sed -n '/<script>/,/<\\/script>/p' prototype.html | sed '1d;$d' > /tmp/p.js &…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[103.65, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I've built the prototype as one self-contained file, `<workspace>/prototype.html`. Double-click it to open\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it in any browser. It shows as a phone-sized frame on desktop and fills the screen on mobile. I haven't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  opened it in a browser. I only checked that the JavaScript parses without errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  It covers the MVP screens from `plan.md`, with fake data held in memory:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Sign-in and onboarding:** Email, Apple and Google buttons all sign you in. A welcome sheet then asks for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  road or gravel and mentions the privacy zone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Feed:** Ride cards have a map thumbnail, kudos toggle and comments. Tapping one opens the ride detail\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with comments and its segments.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Segments:** Each has a map, stats and leaderboard tabs for Friends, Club and Local.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Record:** Pick road or gravel, then start, pause, resume and finish. The timer and live stats tick while\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  you ride. Finishing lets you name and save the ride. It then shows XP earned, streak, challenge and segment\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  results, a badge unlock, and a level-up when you cross one. The saved ride appears in the feed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Challenges:** Joined challenges show progress bars that update after a ride. You can join more and buy a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  streak-freeze token with XP.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Clubs:** You can join or leave a club and post to its feed. A club-vs-club banner is at the top.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Profile:** XP and level, badges, bike garage and privacy settings.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pro paywall:** The Pro-only items are blurred until you unlock them from the paywall, which has monthly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and annual options and a trial button. They are the ride power analysis, profile training insights, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  premium Gravel Grinder challenge, and club admin tools. Recording, feed, segments and basic clubs stay free,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  as the plan says.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The left panel has \"Reset\" and \"Trigger push\" buttons. Reset restores the starting state, and the push\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  button shows a sample notification toast.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The maps are generated SVG routes, not real map tiles. Territory capture and the other v2 features are left\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  out.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[103.755, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Before you finish:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +286 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
