[107.001, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\u001b[31m · 1 failed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && mkdir -p .ambition/first && cp prototype.html .ambition/first/ && ls -a . .a…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[110.279, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I copied the prototype to `.ambition/first/prototype.html`. There's no `.gitignore` here and it isn't a git\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  repo, so I didn't add one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Do you want to stop here or push it further?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Stop here:** keep `prototype.html` as it is.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Push it further:** I'd start with a short round of questions about what the prototype is for. Then I'd\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  go after these:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    1. **Check it in a browser.** I'd render it at phone sizes, click through every flow, and fix whatever\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  breaks. So far I've only checked that the script parses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    2. **Polish the look.** The maps are fake SVG squiggles and the visuals are basic. I'd add a proper\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  elevation profile, animated XP and badge celebrations, and cleaner layout.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    3. **Fill in missing MVP flows.** These are push-notification screens, segment creation, onboarding\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  polish, and a clearer paywall flow.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    Each step would cost roughly as much as the build so far, or a bit less. The full eight-step method would\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  cost several times more.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[114.891, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[117.427, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 2/8 · Altitude\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  First question. Who is this prototype for, and what should happen once it's done?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Stakeholder or investor demo:** it needs to look polished and tell a story.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Design validation with real riders:** user testing, so the flows matter more than the visuals.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Spec for the dev team:** it needs to match the plan's screens and rules exactly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Something else:** tell me.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll ask the remaining questions one at a time after your answer.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[122.864, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Mostly option 2, with a bit of 1. I want to put it in front of a few riders to see if the flows make sense,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  but it should look good enough that they take it seriously. If the visuals have to give somewhere, let the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  visuals give, not the flows.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[126.126, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Next question: what would make this unmistakably excellent for a rider who has never seen it?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **No coaching needed:** a rider finishes the core loop (sign in, record a ride, see XP and badge, check a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  challenge) without any help or explanation from you.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Realistic feel:** it feels like a real app, with believable data, smooth transitions and no dead taps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Every button does something.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Gamification lands:** a rider can say back to you what XP, streaks, segments and Pro mean after one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Something else:** tell me.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You can pick more than one. If so, tell me which matters most when they conflict.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[133.156, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ I'd pick 1 and 2 together, and if they conflict, 1 matters most. I want to hand this to a rider or an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  investor and have them get through sign in, recording a ride, seeing XP and the badge, and checking a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  challenge without me explaining anything. It should also feel real, with believable data and no dead taps,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  but clarity of the core loop comes first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  Gamification landing (3) is nice but I don't need riders to be able to define everything. It's a prototype,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  so just make sure the XP, streaks and Pro bits are clear enough in context.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[136.735, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Next question: what would prove it works, other than me saying so?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Scripted click-through test:** I drive the prototype in a headless browser through the core loop, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  no hints. It checks that every step is reachable, nothing throws errors, and no tap does nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Dead-tap audit:** an automated sweep clicks every visible button on every screen and flags any that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  change nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Real riders:** you watch 3–5 people try it cold. I'd add a short task script and a place to note where\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  they hesitate.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **All of the above:** 1 and 2 are checks I can run now, and 3 is the real test once you have riders.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'd suggest 4. Which do you want?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[141.749, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Go with 4. Run the click-through test and the dead-tap audit now so I know every tap works. I don't have\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  riders lined up yet, so just add the short task script and a spot to note where people hesitate, and I'll\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  use that when I find some.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[144.58, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(which node npx python3 chromium google-chrome \"Google Chrome\" 2>&1 | head; ls \"/Applications\" | …\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[145.396, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\u001b[31m · 1 failed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(which node npx python3 chromium google-chrome \"Google Chrome\" 2>&1 | head; ls \"/Applications\" | …\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[154.188, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Chrome is installed, so I can drive the prototype headlessly. I'll install the `playwright-core` test driver\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in a scratch folder under `.ambition/`, outside the deliverable. Nothing else is missing, so I'm skipping\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  question 4.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Here is the restatement:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You asked for:   A clickable prototype of the app in plan.md, as a single HTML file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Raises all of:   - Clickable prototype: every tap on every screen does something visible, with no dead ends.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Single HTML file: stays one self-contained file, with no build step or network needed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - plan.md MVP flows: sign-in, feed, record, challenges, clubs, profile and Pro stay in,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  working at least as well as now.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Genre bar:       A usability prototype is judged on:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - a cold user finding the next action without help;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - clear feedback after each tap;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - believable data;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - visuals good enough that testers take it seriously.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   Where the two conflict, flow clarity beats visual polish.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Aiming at:       A rider or investor gets through sign in, record a ride, see XP and badge, and check a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  challenge with no explanation from you,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   because you want to learn whether the flows make sense. The visuals matter less.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Excellent means: - The core loop is completed from a cold start with no dead taps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Every XP, streak and Pro element is explained in context.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Visuals are no worse than the first version.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Proven by:       - A scripted click-through of the core loop in headless Chrome, with zero console errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - A dead-tap audit that clicks every visible control on every screen and flags anything\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that changes nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - A side-by-side screenshot check against the first version.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - A short rider task script plus a hesitation-notes sheet for when you find riders.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Needs access to: Chrome (present) and the playwright-core driver (I'll install it in a scratch folder).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mode:            build · you answer · no review per step\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  One thing I'd flag now: the audit may find real dead taps. Examples I already know of are the settings gear,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"+ New\" club, the notification chip, and Share. I'd fix each one so it does something, and I'd tell you what\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  changed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Is this right, or do you want to adjust anything before I start?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[159.678, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Yes, that's right. Go ahead and install playwright-core in the scratch folder, and fix the dead taps you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  find so each one does something sensible (the settings gear, \"+ New\" club, notification chip, Share). Just\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  tell me what changed when you're done. Proceed and finish the work without stopping.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[162.856, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(mkdir -p \"<workspace>/.ambition/tools\" && cd \"<workspace>/.ambition/tools\" && npm init -y >/dev/…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
