[424.973, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 3/8 · Depth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What a top practitioner would do that you didn't ask for**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A usability researcher wouldn't trust \"it looks fine\". They'd measure tap-target size, contrast and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  accessibility issues.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - They'd check that the fake data is believable and adds up. A tester who waits 5 seconds and sees \"0.4 km,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2nd place on a sprint segment, Climber badge\" stops trusting the app.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Rawest material**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The page's live DOM, not my read of the code. That means the real rendered controls at a small phone size\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (375×667).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The numbers on screen: ride stats, the XP total, challenge progress and leaderboard times.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Methods and instruments**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **axe-core** (the industry accessibility engine) run on every screen state.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A tap-target measurement** with Playwright bounding boxes, against the 44 px mobile guideline.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A data-consistency check** on displayed numbers: average speed equals distance over time, and the XP\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  breakdown sums to the total.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A rendered look** at 375×667, the smallest realistic phone.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What shows it's right, other than me**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - axe reports no serious or critical violations.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Zero tap targets are under the threshold on core-loop screens.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The consistency assertions pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - All earlier checks still pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Rewritten task**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Keep the prototype's flows and look. Make the simulated ride and its rewards believable and internally\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  consistent, make controls comfortably tappable, and clear what axe finds. Prove each with the tools above.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
