[692.556, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Step 3 report. The prototype is updated, and a copy is in `.ambition/steps/3/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Measured real usability.** I ran the axe-core accessibility engine, a 44 px tap-target measurement and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  horizontal-overflow check on every screen at 375×667. I also added a data-consistency check,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `consistency.js`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fixed what it found.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Accessibility:** axe went from 17 serious violations (15 colour-contrast, 2 on scrolling areas) to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  none. I darkened the orange button fill, put dark text on the avatars, kept the locked-badge labels\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  readable, and made the scrolling area keyboard-focusable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Tap targets:** controls under 44 px went from 45 to 0.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Small-phone layout:** the Finish and Pause buttons were hidden behind the tab bar while recording, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the \"See my challenges\" button was cut off after a ride. Both now fit at 375×667, which I confirmed by\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  looking at the rendered screens.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Made the ride believable.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Pacing:** the demo ride now runs at 1 second = 1 minute. About 10 seconds gives roughly 4.5 km and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  about 60 XP. Before, 5 seconds gave 0.5 km.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **XP breakdown:** the post-ride sheet shows distance, climbing and a weekly bonus that sum to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  headline XP.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Badge:** it's now \"Fresh Legs\", for the first ride, instead of an absurd \"Climber\" on a flat 0.5 km\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ride.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Segment result:** it only appears for rides of 2 km or more, and the 2nd place matches the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  leaderboard.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The previous step's checks missed the cut-off buttons. They only ran at one size, so a rider on a small\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  phone couldn't have finished a ride without scrolling.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Seeded ride data was already consistent: average speed matches distance over time for all four rides.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Checks run**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - axe: 0 violations. Tap targets under 44 px: 0. Overflow: 0.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Consistency: all 5 pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Click-through: all 13 pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Four-fix check: all 11 pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Dead-tap audit: 15 hits on 180 controls, all re-taps of the tab or segment you're already on.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I removed the tappable \"Start ride\" text in the demo tip. It was too small to tap comfortably, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real button sits right below it. The click-through test now clicks the button.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I updated the rider script to say the ride takes about 10 seconds.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Only Chrome, not Safari or Firefox.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Real devices.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
