[903.958, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What this is really trying to do (verbs)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Get a stranger through the core loop unaided: sign in, ride, see the reward, check a challenge. That's the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  genre's own verb, so it stays.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Look and respond like a real app, so riders take it seriously.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Capture evidence of where people hesitate, instead of relying on someone watching.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Do it without nudging riders into harm, such as unsafe riding, exposing home, or a coercive paywall.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fields, the method I'm borrowing from each, and the direction taken**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Field | What they actually do | Direction taken |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Mobile product designer (the genre's own best practitioner) | Close the loop: every reward points at a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  next action | \"Next up\" line on the post-ride sheet |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Game designer (streak and XP systems) | Show progress toward the next goal right after the reward |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Nearest challenge % and XP to next level |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Usability research ops | Instrument sessions: timestamped taps, task milestones, flagged pauses | A\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  facilitator **Session log** in Settings, covering taps, milestones and pauses of 5 s or more, with no typed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  text |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Aviation human factors (the unusual one) | Guard irreversible actions and design for slips | Confirm\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  before **Discard ride**, and block **Sign out** mid-ride |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Red team: security, privacy and consumer-protection auditor | Break it, misuse it, find who it hurts |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Findings below |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The edge I took:** the Session log. It turns your hesitation notes into evidence you don't have to watch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for. It is built for the riders and investors you'll hand this to, since it makes each handover produce\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  data. That is the direction I weighted most. I'll build the rest around it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Red team: I'll run the attacks before I report them.**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
