[1151.722, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Step 5 report. The prototype is updated, and a copy is in `.ambition/steps/5/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I took methods from four fields and added a red-team pass, as set out above.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Product design:** the post-ride sheet now ends with a \"Next up\" line, for example \"Climb 2,000 m 68% ·\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  114 XP to Level 5\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Game design:** the same line shows XP to the next level.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Research ops:** I built the Session log (Settings → \"Session log (for facilitator)\"). It records\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  timestamped taps, core-loop milestones, the sign-in to challenge-check time, and pauses of 5 s or more, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a Copy button. It records taps only, never anything typed. This replaces most of the hesitation-notes sheet\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  you'd otherwise fill in by hand.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Aviation human factors:** Discard now asks \"Discard this ride?\" with Keep ride as the default. Sign out\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is blocked while a ride is recording.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Red team:** I wrote 20 checks (`redteam.js`) that attack the prototype, ran them, then fixed what broke.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  All 20 pass now.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the red team found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Typed text ran as live markup.** Ride titles, comments, club names and club posts were inserted raw. A\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tester typing `<img onerror=…>` would execute code and could wreck a screen. They're now escaped, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  length limits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Long names overflowed the layout.** A 120-character club name pushed the screen sideways. Fixed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Discard deleted a ride with one tap.** Fixed, as above.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Harms:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Privacy zone:** turning it off silently exposed the home start and end. It now warns first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Paywall:** it had no price after the trial, no cancel information and no \"Not now\". It now has all\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  three.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Streak:** the streak pressure had no counterweight. The explainer now says rest is fine and to use a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  freeze token when sick or injured.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Segments:** segments encourage speeding on public roads, so the segment screen now says to obey\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  traffic laws.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I first considered a coach-mark tour for the first run. I dropped it because the demo tip already does\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that job, and a tour would slow the cold run.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I added one new check script, `redteam.js`. I also changed `fixes.js`, because the privacy zone now asks\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  before turning off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Regression checks:** all earlier suites pass. Axe is clean, tap targets under 44 px are 0, and the dead-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tap audit still shows only the 15 benign re-taps. I looked at the rendered log, paywall and segment screens\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  at 375×667.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - No real riders yet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Chrome only.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I didn't run a person-based test of the log. I tested it by script.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
