[1180.782, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 6/8 · Judge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The outside check, defined before I run it**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Everything is a script or a rendered result, not my opinion.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Original ask, intact:** a coverage run over the text of every screen and sheet, checking each MVP item\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in `plan.md` against what the prototype actually shows. It runs on both the first version and the final.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Core-loop promise (cold rider):** a neutral script that signs in, records, finishes, saves and checks a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  challenge at 375×667. It uses only visible buttons, and it measures whether each key button is actually\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tappable (not covered or off-screen) and how many taps the loop takes. It runs on both versions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Genre bar:** the axe accessibility engine, tap-target size, overflow, dead taps and the injection\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  attack, run on both versions. After that comes a cold read of the whole text, and a rendered look.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Regression:** all earlier suites on the final.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
