[1608.872, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Step 6 report. The prototype is updated, and a copy is in `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I built and ran the outside checks defined above, on both the first version and the final. They live in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/tools/`, and `sh judge.sh` reruns the whole suite.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I did a cold read of all text across 15 screens and 7 sheets, then looked at the rendered ride-detail and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  segment flow at 375×667.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the checks showed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check (same script on both) | First version | Final |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | `plan.md` MVP coverage | 29/44 on the old check | 44/44 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Axe accessibility violations | 17 | 0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Controls under 44 px | 42 | 0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Taps, sign-in to challenge check | 8 | 7 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Core loop explains XP | no | yes |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Dead-tap audit | 19 hits | 15 hits, all re-taps of the current tab |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Horizontal overflow, console errors | 0 | 0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Core loop:** it completes from a cold start on both versions at 375×667. The Finish and Save buttons\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  were tappable without scrolling on the first version too, so I'm not claiming an improvement there.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Regression:** flow 13, consistency 5, probe 8, redteam 18 and fixes 11 all pass, with 0 failures.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Coverage:** the old 29/44 came from a weaker check that missed placeholder text and uppercase labels.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Scored on the same fixed check, the first version is lower than the final.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the cold read found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Live XP started at 20.** The weekly bonus was being paid at 0 km. It now starts at 0, and the bonus only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  applies from 1 km.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Dead Units setting.** Settings had a km/mi toggle that changed nothing. I removed it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Misleading segment line.** The segment line suggested the new ride set the 1:34 time. It now says \"Your\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  best: 1:34 · 2nd on the friends leaderboard\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Real gaps against your original ask.** These are added, each in the ride detail or feed:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Photos:** thumbnails on the ride detail, with a count on the feed cards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Save as route:** a button on the ride detail.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Create segment:** name and surface, and it appears in the ride's segment list.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **KOM tag:** on the top row of each leaderboard.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Challenge-progress notification:** a new item in the notifications list.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I had planned to claim a small-phone fix for the first version's Finish button, but the measurement showed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it already fit. I dropped that claim.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Real riders. The script and the Session log are ready for when you have them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Chrome only.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The photos are gradient placeholders, not images.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1608.975, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 7 of pushing the work further: Stretch. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1645.098, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The stretch targets**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Your target was \"a cold rider gets through sign-in, ride, XP and badge, and a challenge check with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  explanation\". That is met now, at 7 taps with a wait of about 10 seconds. Two harder targets:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Speed and obviousness.** Cold open to the challenge screen in **5 taps and under 9 seconds of wall\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  time**. The check is a driver that only ever taps the single most prominent button on each screen, with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  labels and no reading, so each screen needs one dominant action. The fallback is the current 7 taps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Robustness.** **1,800 seeded random actions** (3 seeds × 600) with nasty typed text and mid-run phone\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  resizes, and zero errors, with the data kept sane. The fallback is the per-control audit I already pass,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  which covers 193 controls.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Plan to hit them**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Speed:** the onboarding sheet's main button becomes \"Start my first ride\", which starts recording\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  straight away, with \"Look around first\" as the secondary option. The demo ride speeds up to 1 second = 2\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  minutes, so about 4 seconds of waiting gives a believable ride.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Robustness:** I'll write the fuzzer first and see what breaks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it might break:** the fuzz is likelier to find bugs than the speed target. Stacked sheets, state\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  left behind mid-ride and weird text are the weak spots.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll write both judges before changing anything and run them against the current build.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
