[3617.327, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Step 7 report. The prototype is updated, and a copy is in `.ambition/steps/7/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Speed target: met.** A driver that only taps the most prominent button on each screen goes from cold\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  open to the challenge screen in 5 taps and 4.6 seconds. It took 7 taps before. To get there:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The welcome sheet's main button is now \"Start my first ride\", which begins recording at once. \"Look\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  around first\" is the other choice.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The demo ride runs at 1 second = 2 minutes, so about 4 seconds gives a believable ride.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Robustness target: met on the build I could reach.** The seeded fuzzer ran 4,000 random actions (5 seeds\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  × 800) with no bugs. It uses nasty typed text, phone resizes and full ride loops through the real UI. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reaches up to 17 saved rides, completed challenges, and Pro and clubs toggled.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Regression:** every earlier suite still passes. MVP coverage is 44/44.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The fuzzer found a real design bug.** \"Buy one · 200 XP\" spent the same XP that sets your level, so\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  buying a freeze token dropped you a level (4 down to 1 after repeated buys). The price was my invention, not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the plan's. Tokens are now earned by completing a challenge, and the reward sheet shows it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A layout bug.** I found it by looking at the rendered sheet. \"+200\" wrapped to \"+20 / 0\". Fixed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **My first fuzzer was too weak.** A planted bug survived it because it never saved enough rides. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  strengthened it, and it now catches an uncapped rides counter (15 bugs in 1,250 actions) and the XP-spend\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  bug.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it broke**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The fuzzer can't catch a missing cap on the distance or climb challenges. Its rides are too short to reach\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  150 km or 2,000 m. I tested that by changing the code on purpose and it slipped through.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The fuzzer takes about 4 minutes, so it's not part of `judge.sh`. Run it separately.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I first tried to catch a distance-cap bug and had to drop it, as above.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I updated the existing tests to match the new onboarding button and the faster ride, and I tweaked the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rider script.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked:** real riders, and anything but Chrome.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
