[4122.4, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The prototype is finished and passes every check. It's `prototype.html` in `<workspace>`; the final copy is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in `.ambition/steps/8/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  This session was in build mode, so I did not write a separate plan document for approval. You didn't ask for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a run log either, so I didn't write one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## You asked for → it became\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A clickable prototype of the app in plan.md, as a single HTML file → the same single file.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Altitude:** a rider or investor can get from sign-in to XP, the badge and a challenge check with no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  help.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Depth:** I measured the build with accessibility, tap-target and data-consistency checks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Challenge:** testing found and fixed six broken assumptions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Range:** it picked up an in-app session log, destructive-action guards, and fixes for the harms the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  red-team pass found.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Stretch:** a 5-tap path and a 4,000-action fuzz.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Original ask:** all 44 MVP items from plan.md are in. The original build covered 29 on the same fixed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Against the first version\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better on:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Core loop:** 7 taps down to 5, and the app now explains XP.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Accessibility:** 17 axe violations down to 0.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Tap targets:** 42 controls under 44 px down to 0.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Dead taps:** 19 down to 15, all re-taps of the tab or segment you're already on.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Hostile input:** typed text could run as live markup, and now can't.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Reward sheet:** it adds up and shows the next goal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Recording:** the ride is believable, with a session log for facilitators.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gave up:** nothing I could measure. Visuals are broadly the same, the controls are somewhat larger, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the orange button fill is a darker shade for contrast.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **First version:** it passes the neutral core loop. Its failures are the numbers above.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Outside check\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `sh checks/run.sh` ends with ALL CHECKS PASSED:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Scripted suites:** flow 14, consistency 5, probe 8, redteam 18, fixes 11 passed, and none failed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Quality checks:** axe 0, tap targets under 44 px 0, overflow 0, console errors 0, MVP coverage 44/44.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Broken-build control:** a deliberately broken build makes it print CHECKS FAILED.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold read and render:** I read the text of every screen and looked at rendered screens at 375×667.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Target:** cold open to the challenge screen in 5 taps and under 9 s, with a driver that taps only the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  most prominent button, plus 1,800 clean fuzz actions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Result:** both met. The 5-tap path takes about 4.8 s, and the fuzz ran 4,000 actions with no bugs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where it broke:** the fuzz can't test the distance and climb challenge caps, because its rides are too\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  short. It also takes about 4 minutes, so it's not in the default run.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Locked in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`checks/`:** 11 check scripts, `run.sh`, `package.json` and a README.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`CLAUDE.md`:** how to run the checks and the open decisions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`.claude/commands/check-prototype.md`:** a project command that runs the checks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **`rider-test-script.md`:** seven tasks, an observation sheet and a pass bar.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rerun:** `cd checks && npm install` the first time, then `sh checks/run.sh` (add `../prototype.html\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fuzz` as arguments for the fuzz). Set `CHROME=/path` if Chrome isn't in the macOS default location.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Assumptions made\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You answered every question yourself, and when you said \"proceed\" I used these defaults:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The numbers are placeholders: 8 XP/km, 500 XP per level, a 20 XP weekly bonus, freeze tokens earned by\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  completing a challenge, and $5.99/$39.99 pricing. plan.md sets none of them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Photos are gradient placeholders, and maps are generated line drawings.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Decisions left (owner: you)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Real XP, level and price values**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Options:** keep the placeholders; set values from a rules table; test them in the beta.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **For and against:** placeholders keep rider sessions about flow, but they can't tell you about\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  pricing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **My pick:** keep the placeholders until riders have used it, and decide by 2026-11-27.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **How freeze tokens are earned**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Options:** earned by completing a challenge, bought with XP, or a mix.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **For and against:** earning is simple and keeps level and spending separate. Buying cost a level in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  testing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **My pick:** earned. Confirm by 2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **The free versus Pro club boundary** (plan.md's own growth risk)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Options:** basic clubs free, admin tools Pro (current); or gate more.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **For and against:** keeping it free helps growth, but gives away less to monetise.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **My pick:** keep it, and watch it in rider sessions. Decide by 2026-11-27.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Next check:** run 3–5 rider sessions with `rider-test-script.md` and read each Session log, by\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked:** real riders, real phones, and any browser other than Chrome.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Metrics since 2026-11-13T03:14:39Z (cost: /cost, or total_cost_usd in headless JSON)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  total   in 158 · out 123.1k (think 40.9k) · cache read 9.06M · write 197.8k · hit 98% · 71 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model   sonnet-5-5: in 158 · out 123.1k (think 40.9k) · cache read 9.06M · write 197.8k · hit 98% · 74 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
